From: enjihn <150061999+enjihn@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] color: scale SDR white on Gamma 2.2 HDR output

Apply the compositor SDR-on-HDR white level to traditional Gamma 2.2 HDR
outputs by scaling SDR input against the panel peak, so the SDR content
brightness control is not a no-op there. Ordinary SDR and external PQ
output keep their existing paths.

A Gamma 2.2 HDR output stays enabled while gamescope composites nothing but
SDR, so gate the scale on the focused app actually requesting HDR. Without
that gate every SDR frame is pinned at the SDR-on-HDR white level, which
costs the panel most of its code range and shows up as reduced maximum
brightness and washed out colour at low backlight.

The gate keys on the current base layer, not on every composited layer. An
outgoing HDR base is still painted as HELD_COMMIT_FADE after the new SDR base
takes over, so SDR layers encode unscaled for the fade duration.

diff --git a/src/HDRGamma22.h b/src/HDRGamma22.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..65f4150b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/HDRGamma22.h
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+#pragma once
+
+#include "color_helpers.h"
+
+#include <limits>
+
+namespace gamescope
+{
+    constexpr bool ColorMgmtLutsAreCurrent(
+        bool bColorMgmtConfigCurrent,
+        bool bLutsInitialized,
+        bool bCachedScaleSDRWhite,
+        bool bScaleSDRWhite )
+    {
+        return bColorMgmtConfigCurrent && bLutsInitialized &&
+            bCachedScaleSDRWhite == bScaleSDRWhite;
+    }
+
+    // The output stays in HDR with SDR content, so key on the focused app. An
+    // outgoing HDR base still composites through the fade.
+    constexpr bool ShouldScaleGamma22SDRWhite(
+        bool bOutputHDREnabled,
+        bool bAppWantsHDR,
+        bool bOutputIsHDRG22 )
+    {
+        return bOutputHDREnabled && bAppWantsHDR && bOutputIsHDRG22;
+    }
+
+    // PQ encodes SDR white in its transfer function; Gamma 2.2 does not.
+    constexpr float Gamma22HdrSDRInputScale(
+        bool bScaleSDRWhite,
+        EOTF eOutputEncodingEOTF,
+        float flSDRWhiteNits,
+        float flPanelPeakNits )
+    {
+        if ( !bScaleSDRWhite || eOutputEncodingEOTF != EOTF_Gamma22 ||
+             !( flSDRWhiteNits >= 1.0f ) ||
+             !( flSDRWhiteNits <= std::numeric_limits<float>::max() ) ||
+             !( flPanelPeakNits >= 1.0f ) ||
+             !( flPanelPeakNits <= std::numeric_limits<float>::max() ) )
+        {
+            return 1.0f;
+        }
+
+        const float flClampedSDRWhiteNits = flSDRWhiteNits < flPanelPeakNits
+            ? flSDRWhiteNits
+            : flPanelPeakNits;
+        return flClampedSDRWhiteNits / flPanelPeakNits;
+    }
+}
